/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The IR flame sensor is used to detect fire or flame by sensing infrared radiation emitted by it. Flames emit infrared light in the wavelength range of approximately 760nm to 1100nm, which is detected by the sensor. The module typically has four pins: VCC, GND, Digital Output \(DO\), and Analog Output \(AO\). In this project, the digital output is connected to the Arduino. When flame is detected, the output signal changes state, which is then read by the Arduino to trigger the alarm system.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
